# Token Saving Rules

## Navigation
- ALWAYS use `get_function` or `find_symbol` (Token Savior MCP) instead of reading whole files
- Read only the specific lines needed, never entire files unless absolutely required
- Use `search_codebase` for finding patterns instead of reading multiple files

## Code Generation
- Show only changed sections in edits, not full file rewrites
- Abstract repeated patterns before implementing — DRY is also token-DRY
- Prefer targeted StrReplace edits over Write (full file) when possible

## Context Management
- Do not re-read files that were just written — trust what was written
- Reference previously discussed decisions without re-explaining them
- Keep responses minimal: code + one-line explanation, no essays

## Architecture Rules (ZenFlowAI)
- Resolvers call services only. Services call Prisma only. No business logic in resolvers.
- One module = one responsibility. No cross-module internal imports.
- All shared utilities live in lib/ (frontend) or utils/ (backend)
- Types are always explicit. No `any`. No implicit returns.
- Every new function must be pure if possible (no side effects = easy to test)
